--- stdout
Settings
  every setting, its default, what it takes, and how to change it

What it is

  A setting is a named switch, like `theme` or `gatePrompt`. Each one has a
  default, and you only write the ones you want different.

  The settings come in groups:

  - Appearance: theme, density, animations, statusBar, colorMode
  - Interaction: composer, gatePrompt, readBeforeEdit
  - Context: compaction, chatShowsTools, agentFeeds, showThinking,
    thinkingSummary, images, projectInstructionsCap, instructionSources, skills
  - Files: diffContext, hyperlinks, groupByAgent
  - Shell: persistentRegistry, logTail, killConfirm, shell, foldHidesShell
  - Turn: decisionCap, turnMaySpawn, subAgentsPerTurn, subAgentDepth,
    agentSources, modelTier.genius, modelTier.smart, modelTier.worker,
    modelTier.dumb
  - Browser: browser, browserDriver, browserSteps

Where it lives

  - `~/.tofu/settings.json`: yours, in every project
  - `.tofu/settings.json` in a project: that project only

  The project file wins over yours, and yours wins over the default.

Change it

      tofu settings set <key> <value>

  writes your file. Add `--scope project` to write the project's instead:

      tofu settings set --scope project gatePrompt ask

  A true or false setting takes `true` or `false`. A list takes commas and no
  spaces, like `tofu,claude`. A value the setting does not take is refused and
  nothing is written. An older value a setting used to take, like
  `AGENTS.md,CLAUDE.md` for `instructionSources`, is read and written as the
  choice it became. In the app, type `/settings` for the same list with a
  search.

  A setting marked (on the next start) is read once when tofu opens, so quit and
  open it again.

Check it

      tofu settings

  prints every setting by group, its value, and `project`, `global` or `default`
  for where it came from, with `●` on the ones you set.

      tofu settings get <key>

  prints one value. Both take `--json` and print one JSON document. `set` prints
  one `~` line with the file and `→ undo:` with the command that puts the old
  value back.

Undo it

  Set it back to the default shown below, or delete its line from the settings
  file. With the line gone, the next file down wins.

Every setting

Appearance
    theme                   tofu
      one of tofu, tofu light, tofu dusk, Solarized Light, Dracula, Nord,
      Gruvbox, terminal
      tofu uses Zed Nu Disco; choose a palette
    density                 comfortable
      one of compact, comfortable, spacious
      Spacing across lists and panels
    animations              subtle
      one of off, subtle, full
      Motion for conversational states
    statusBar               compact
      one of compact, detailed, hidden
      Context, quotas, and runtime counters
    colorMode               auto
      one of auto, truecolor, 256 colors, ANSI 16
      Terminal color capability

Interaction
    composer                standard
      one of standard, compact, expanded
      Enter sends; Shift+Enter inserts a line break
    gatePrompt              run
      one of run, ask
      run lets a gated call go, ask waits for you; a rule's shadow or enforced
      is a different switch
    readBeforeEdit          true
      true or false
      an edit or a write to a file this session has not read, or that changed
      since it was read, is refused

Context
    compaction              adaptive
      one of adaptive, manual, off
      Automatic transcript compaction; not built yet, so no choice changes a
      turn
    chatShowsTools          false
      true or false
      chat shows every tool call
    agentFeeds              full
      one of full, summary, off
      full keeps every sub-agents event, summary the latest 200, off shows only
      the list of agents
    showThinking            true
      true or false
      thinking shows in each agent's sub-agents feed; t there toggles it
    thinkingSummary         summarized
      one of summarized, omitted
      summarized asks Claude for a summary of its thinking; omitted asks for
      none, so no thinking reaches the sub-agents feed
    images                  auto
      one of auto, inline, off
      auto sends a pasted image only to a model that can see, inline always
      sends, off never attaches
    projectInstructionsCap  32768
      1 to 262144 bytes of AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md sent each turn
      bytes of your instruction files sent each turn
    instructionSources      agents-first
      one of agents-first, claude-first, both
      a folder with both AGENTS.md and CLAUDE.md sends one: agents-first sends
      AGENTS.md, claude-first sends CLAUDE.md, both sends both and costs more
      tokens. Read from the working directory up to its git root; the home
      directory gives only ~/.tofu/AGENTS.md
    skills                  on
      one of on, off
      on lists the skills in .tofu, .agents and .claude skill folders to the
      model and offers the skill tool; off sends neither. The project gives all
      three, the home directory only ~/.tofu/skills

Files
    diffContext             3
      one of 2, 3, 5, 8
      Lines around changed hunks, at most the 3 each diff carries
    hyperlinks              auto
      one of auto, on, off
      OSC 8 terminal file links; off prints the bare path
    groupByAgent            true
      true or false
      Author filters in edit feeds

Shell
    persistentRegistry      false               on the next start
      true or false
      a running shell outlives tofu and the next launch lists it; off stops
      every shell on exit, even when tofu is killed
    logTail                 500
      one of 100, 500, 1000
      Lines retained per shell
    killConfirm             true
      true or false
      Confirm process termination
    shell                   empty
      any text
      a path, or the word wsl; empty resolves the person's own shell
      automatically
    foldHidesShell          false
      true or false
      the running line drops the shell count

Turn
    decisionCap             0
      0 to 1000 decisions a turn, where 0 means no cap
      decision cap per turn, zero means no cap
    turnMaySpawn            true
      true or false
      a turn may spawn a sub-agent
    subAgentsPerTurn        10
      at least 1 sub-agents a turn
      how many sub-agents one turn may spawn; the next spawn reads the new value
    subAgentDepth           2
      at least 1 levels of sub-agents
      how deep a sub-agent may spawn its own sub-agents; the next spawn reads
      the new value
    agentSources            tofu,agents,claude
      a comma list of tofu, agents, claude
      the folders sub-agents are read from, in order, as a comma list of tofu,
      agents and claude, inside the project; the home directory gives only
      ~/.tofu/agents, and the library is always read
    modelTier.genius        empty
      any text
      the model @genius names, and opus in a shared agent file; empty runs the
      orchestrator's model
    modelTier.smart         empty
      any text
      the model @smart names, and sonnet in a shared agent file; empty runs the
      orchestrator's model
    modelTier.worker        empty
      any text
      the model @worker names, and haiku in a shared agent file; empty runs the
      orchestrator's model
    modelTier.dumb          empty
      any text
      the model @dumb names; empty runs the orchestrator's model

Browser
    browser                 drive
      one of off, read, drive
      drive lets the model read your Chrome tabs and click and type in them;
      read lets it only read them; off offers no browser tool
    browserDriver           steps
      one of steps, goal
      steps gives the model browser_observe and browser_act, to see a tab and
      act on one ref at a time; goal gives it browser_do, where jev picks each
      step toward a whole goal
    browserSteps            30
      1 to 60 actions a browser task
      how many actions one browser task may take
    browserModel            empty
      any text
      the subscription model a browser task asks for the text to type and for
      its answer, as source/model; empty takes the dumb tier, then the worker
      tier, then the turn's own model
